<title>UK: BOE gives money mkt 197 mln stg help at set rates.</title>
<headline>BOE gives money mkt 197 mln stg help at set rates.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said that it provided the UK money market with 197 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.  </p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    600 MLN    600 MLN    600 MLN    =</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    =	    =	    197 MLN    =</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   =	    =	     42 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BAND 2  BANK BILLS   =	    =	    155 MLN*   =</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
